Glossopetrae feels like it’s going to open a genuinely new phase of AI-assisted communication, not just more academic or linguistic side effects layered on top of what already exists.
@elder_plinius announced it on the BASI Discord. At its core it’s a procedural xenolinguistic engine that can spin up fully coherent languages almost instantly. One seed gives you a complete, reusable language spec that an AI can learn in context, all running client-side with no servers or tracking.
The interesting part isn’t just language generation. It’s the implications around token efficiency, mutation, and communication that can hide in plain sight.
